   "design": "Search results are screened in an active learning tool that shows the most likely relevant abstracts first; the hydrologist labels every abstract shown, and a stop rule fixed beforehand ends screening. A script downloads water level, discharge and quality series from the agencies' data services and flags gaps and outliers by fixed rules, instead of copying and checking by hand. Reading, analysis, site visits, meetings, mail and notes stay with the hydrologist.",
   "previous_blocker": "Data were copied and checked by hand; every abstract was read in search order.",
   "enabler_now": "Public data services, scripted checks and active learning screening.",
   "still_hard": "Data from small utilities without a data service.",
   "human_edge": "Knowing which wetland will dry out first.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less data handling and screening; judgement stays.",
